    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d264">

                <pb facs="0386" n="364" sameAs="frus:frus1951v02/pg364"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">310.2/10–2445: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Representative at the United
                        Nations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Austin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-10-24T16:19:00-05:00">October 24,
                            1951—4:19 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>526. Be Italian Membership: Italian observer Guidotti on instructions saw Gross
                    this morning and voiced Italian Govt’s “keen disappointment” that Guidotti had
                    been told by Hickerson we had no suggestions to offer re Italian membership
                    beyond what Guidotti called, “undoubtedly useless”, step of renewed SC
                    discussion membership question. He said in tripartite declaration we had
                    indicated we <pb facs="0387" n="365" xml:id="pg365"/> would take all steps
                    possible to aid Italy and we should do just that even if it meant “stretching
                    the charter a little”.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Austin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
